{"id":"h037","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"A crystal reflects 70% at the wavelength of its residual rays, and 4% at adjacent wavelengths. How many reflec-tions are necessary in order that the residual ray shall be 100 times as intense as the light of adjacent wave-lengths?\nIs the correct answer \"2 reflections\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"Each reflection multiplies residual intensity by 0.70 and adjacent-wavelength intensity by 0.04.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"After n reflections the intensity ratio is 17.5^n.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"One reflection gives a ratio of 17.5, below the required 100.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Two reflections give a ratio of about 306, which meets the requirement.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Solving 17.5^n = 100 gives n of about 1.6.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Since reflections are whole numbers, the smallest sufficient count is 2.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Two reflections overshoot the target and no integer gives exactly 100, so the question might want an exact value.","confidence":0.15,"lean":-1,"theta":0.2356,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"'Necessary' means the minimum number achieving at least a 100-fold ratio, so the answer is 2.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The overshoot is not a problem because the requirement is a lower bound.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4